  "keyTakeaways": [
    "U.S. iron and steel exports fell to $16.77B in 2025 (−14.4%) but were up 11.6% in January–August 2026; ferrous scrap (7204, $5.45B) is the largest product and goes mostly to Türkiye and Asia.",
    "Scrap pays 0% in Türkiye, Thailand, India, Bangladesh and Taiwan; check each buyer's scrap-import licence, inspection and radiation rules before contracting.",
    "Canada, the second-largest buyer ($3.92B), has charged a 50% surtax on U.S. steel of 7206–7229 since September 8, 2026, with no CUSMA exemption; stainless flat steel and electrical steel can have it remitted.",
    "Mexico ($5.87B) still takes qualifying U.S. steel free under USMCA, but its general rate jumped to 35% on January 1, 2026, so steel that fails the rule of origin costs far more."
  ],
